--- body ---
## Context

Found live, by the author, testing v0.3.15 (ticket 0742's persisted switch)
right after install: turning indexing off left the dialog's overall-progress
bar visibly animating, as if work were still under way.

## Root cause

`getSDTCoverage()`'s `known` flag governs whether the dialog's
`sdt-global-progress` element gets a `value` attribute. Off census
(`duringCensus` false), `known` required `state.scanned === state.total`.
Switching off before a census finishes — the ordinary case, since a user
reaches for the switch precisely while indexing is running — leaves that
false forever: nothing moves `scanned` or `total` again once off. So
`<progress>` never gets a `value` attribute, which makes it indeterminate,
which the platform renders with its own native, continuously looping
animation — independent of the 100 ms `render()` pulse, which `disarmSDTSitter()`
already clears correctly. The loop being stopped proved nothing; the bug
was never in the loop.

## Fix

`getSDTCoverage()` now also treats `state.phase === 'switched-off'` as
"known": once off, the counts are frozen, not merely stalled, so the bar
should read a settled number rather than stay unsayable.

## Test

`tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs`, "switching off mid-census freezes the
progress bar instead of leaving it animating" — sets `scanned`/`total` to an
unfinished split, fires the switch off, and asserts the progress element
carries a `value`. Verified red against the unfixed code (positive control,
via `git stash`) and green after.

## Verification

- [x] `tests/sdt_sitter_dialog.mjs` — new arm, reddens on the unfixed code
- [x] `tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs`, `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs`,
      `tests/sdt_sitter_startup.mjs` — unaffected, still pass
- [x] `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` — 54 passed

## Exit criteria

Switching indexing off while a census is incomplete leaves the dialog's
overall-progress bar at a fixed, non-animating value.
